# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Extensionless Linux/macOS binary from `go build -o pigeonpost .` (root-anchored so it
# never matches the tracked pigeonpost.png)
/pigeonpost

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
*.cov
# Stray ad-hoc coverage profile from a manual `go test -coverprofile=...`
# (test.ps1 itself writes to %TEMP%, never the repo)
$coverProfile

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.claude/

# macOS filesystem junk
.DS_Store

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
# Vitest coverage output
frontend/coverage/
# Wails npm dependency-hash cache (regenerated on every build)
frontend/package.json.md5
# Wails Go->JS bindings, regenerated by `wails build` on every run
frontend/wailsjs/
installer/frontend/wailsjs/

# Wails build output
build/bin/

# The image assets `go run ./tools/genicons` derives are TRACKED, deliberately, and nothing here
# ignores them. Only build.ps1, builddmg.sh and build_flatpak.sh run the generator; wails.json has no
# hook, so `wails dev` and a bare `wails build` (both documented in DEVELOPMENT-README.md) run it
# never. An asset the front end imports has to be in a fresh clone already or the build cannot resolve
# it, which was measured: with the glyphs absent, vite fails on src/icons.ts. These paths were listed
# here for a while and had no effect at all, since a rule cannot ignore a file git already tracks.
# The single exception is genicons' flatpak hicolor set, ignored under the flatpak artefacts below:
# nothing reads it but build_flatpak.sh, which generates it first.

# macOS DMG build output
dist-dmg/
PigeonPost.dmg
# create-dmg leaves a read-write scratch image behind if interrupted.
rw.*.dmg

# Windows installer build output (build.ps1)
dist-installer/
installer/build/bin/
installer/payload.zip

# Flatpak build artefacts (regenerated by build_flatpak.sh)
.flatpak-build/
.flatpak-repo/
.flatpak-builder/
packaging/
*.flatpak
uk.codecrafter.PigeonPost.yml
build/linux/

# Local scratch
NOTES.md
*.db
*.db-*

# transient parking folder for files the Claude device bridge cannot delete
_to_delete/

# Stray root package-lock.json created when npm runs in repo root during wails generate module
/package-lock.json
